Independent GrokBot sealed review transport audit 966e 20261029: cloud run finished before its SDK stream closed; accepting terminal status
{"approved":true,"findings":[{"severity":"low","file":"scripts/lib/grokbot-dispatch-work.mjs","line":79,"problem":"A reviewer mismatch is reported with requireValue, which throws, instead of returning false: `requireValue(typeof reviewerAgentId==='string'&&...&&pending[0].reviewerAgentId===reviewerAgentId,'Sealed reviewer does not match the actual roster agent receiving this job')`. The throw escapes dispatchApprovedWork's `for (const job of jobs)` loop, and no 'not-dispatchable' receipt is saved.","trigger":"A manifest contains a sealed-review ticket for grokbot-24 whose registered reviewerAgentId differs from grokbot-24's roster/persisted agentId, followed by a valid extraction ticket for grokbot-25 (when maxActive allows two selections).","consequence":"Every cycle until the ticket expires (at most one hour) aborts at the review ticket. It repeats the MCP status call and never reaches the later valid ticket. The dispatcher fails closed and sends nothing wrong, but other approved work is delayed.","requiredFix":"Keep refusing the wake, but persist a 'not-dispatchable' receipt with reason 'reviewer-mismatch', or skip just that ticket, so later jobs in the cycle are still processed. Add a dispatcher test where the IDs mismatch and assert that no wake happens and no reservation is made. The supplied sealed-review test only exercises matching IDs."},{"severity":"low","file":"scripts/grokbot-review-jobs.mjs","line":19,"problem":"The host-side sticky-work guard calls `readRemotePeopleWorkLedger()` with no queue options and without fetchPeopleQueueBase. The bridge, by contrast, uses `readRemotePeopleWorkLedger(queueOptions(this.options))` after a fetch. The guard also treats any dateAudits entry with `status!=='ready'` as blocking.","trigger":"Either the local remote-tracking ledger ref is older than a claim another host just made, or the worker has historic dateAudits entries in terminal statuses other than 'ready' (for example submitted or released).","consequence":"In the stale case, a review can be registered for a worker that does hold a sticky extraction. Because of the bridge fix this no longer deadlocks: the sticky resume still works and the review waits. In the terminal-status case, registration is refused for that worker indefinitely. Both outcomes fail safe; neither loses work.","requiredFix":"Fetch and read the ledger with the same queue options the bridge uses, and test only active date-audit statuses (the claimIsActive-equivalent), not `!=='ready'`."},{"severity":"low","file":"scripts/test-grokbot-review-store.mjs","line":49,"problem":"The new sticky-recovery regression test writes fixture assignment, packet and output files into the real shared checkout through `assignmentDirectory(j.worker,target)` with `fs.mkdirSync(dir,{recursive:true})`. Cleanup removes only the leaf directory.","trigger":"Running the test suite in the shared host checkout, especially if the run is interrupted before t.after runs.","consequence":"Empty parent directories are left for the fake worker 'grokbot-sticky-test-<pid>', or full fixture files if the run is killed, inside data/people/generated in the checkout every worker shares. The test checks that the directory does not already exist, so existing work is never clobbered.","requiredFix":"Point the assignment helpers at a temporary root through an injectable option or environment override, or remove every directory the test created."}]}
